* Precision reference subsystem using ADR1399H and LTC6078
* Load required libraries
.lib ADR1399H.sub
.lib LTC6078.sub

* Primary Input Supply (15V)
V1 IN 0 15

* ADR1399H Zener Bias
* 2.67k resistor from 15V provides ~3mA bias current to the Zener
R1 IN Z_plus 2.67k
* ADR1399H Connections: Zener+, Zener-, Heater+, Heater-
* Heater is powered directly from the 15V input supply
X1 Z_plus 0 IN 0 ADR1399H

* Op-Amp Power Supplies
* The LTC6078 is a 5V max precision op-amp. To safely buffer a 7.05V reference, 
* we generate a floating 5V supply that perfectly tracks the Zener voltage.
* This ensures the op-amp sees exactly 5V across its supply pins and operates 
* with the input perfectly centered in its common-mode range.
E1 VCC_OP_base 0 Z_plus 0 1
V2 VCC_OP VCC_OP_base 2.5
E2 VEE_OP_base 0 Z_plus 0 1
V3 VEE_OP_base VEE_OP 2.5

* LTC6078 Unity-Gain Buffer
* Pin order: IN+, IN-, V+, V-, OUT
X2 Z_plus OUT VCC_OP VEE_OP OUT LTC6078

* Load (1 kOhm)
Rload OUT 0 1k

* Analysis Directive (Transient analysis to allow DC operating point to settle)
.tran 10m

.end
